This folio (149v) contains no mathematics and no handwriting by Riemann. It is page 8 (the advertising section headed 'AZIENDA') of the Turin daily 'Il Conte Cavour', no. 140, which ran from 5 to 6 July 1865. The previous page (p. 7, with news dispatches and Borsa quotations dated 3–5 July 1865) and the next page (front page of no. 141, Thursday 6 July 1865) belong to the same newspaper. The sheet was presumably kept in the bundle as a wrapper or as scrap paper, consistent with Riemann's stay in Italy in 1865.

The printed content consists of:
(1) a Holloway's Pills and Ointment patent-medicine advertisement, sold by 'Professore Holloway, Londra, Strada, Num. 244';
(2) an advertisement for Borgetti Gioachino, a contractor for gas and water piping, via Lagrange 2, Turin;
(3) a notice of a treatise on silk-cocoon reeling by G. B. Debernardi, price L. 5;
(4) an 'Avviso' offering a director/actor to amateur dramatic societies, with replies to 'E. O.' at the Teatro Balbo;
(5) a situation-wanted notice from a 40-year-old married person seeking a porter's post;
(6) a letter dated Genova, 4 luglio 1865, from Eleuterio Cerbone[?] protesting that a proposed Turin urban-rent insurance company copies his own Genoa company (founded 20 Feb 1865, authorized by Royal Decree 17 Apr 1865);
(7) a notice from the Tipografia del Conte Cavour of the Regolamento for the new Legge Comunale, dated 8 giugno 1865, price 20 centesimi.

There are no derivations, formulas, figures, or marginal annotations to reconstruct.
